{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS1LbNST7TxDwTTxfyxa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've added all six events from `docs/EVENTS.md` to the registration and offers screens. They all go through `Analytics.capture`, with the exact names and properties from the spec, and the email and phone number are never sent. `flutter analyze` reports no issues, but I haven't run the app, so how often each event fires hasn't been tested at runtime.\n\n**What each event does:**\n- **`registration_email_started` / `registration_phone_started`:** fire once per screen visit, on the first edit. A flag on the screen state stops them firing on every keystroke.\n- **`loan_amount_changed`:** fires once when the user lets go of the slider, rather than on every step of a drag. It sends `amount` as an int.\n- **`terms_accepted`:** fires only when the box goes from unticked to ticked.\n- **`registration_continue_tapped`:** fires on each tap, before going to the offers screen, with `amount` and `terms`.\n- **`offers_scrolled`:** fires once at the end of each scroll, sending how far the list was scrolled as `offset`.\n\n**The colleague's note:** It fits this app, which is Flutter on the PostHog free tier, billed per event. The spec's wording (\"started typing\", \"moved the slider\", \"scrolled\") would have led to exactly the problem the note describes. I used its once-per-visit flags for text fields, the release-only slider event, the end-of-scroll event and keeping names and properties unchanged. Two parts didn't apply: the focus-handler steps, because no event needs a field's final value, and its debug-log check, because I didn't run the app. ANSWER.md lists which parts applied and suggests running that check on a debug build.\n\n**Two choices you might want to change:**\n- `offers_scrolled` fires once per scroll, not once per visit. If the event budget is tight, you could send one event with the furthest scroll position when the user leaves the screen. On tall screens the 10-offer list may not scroll at all, so those users can never reach that last funnel step.\n- `terms_accepted` fires again if the user unticks and re-ticks the box.\n\nRunning `flutter analyze` made the Flutter tool rewrite `analysis_options.yaml` and create `.dart_tool/` and `pubspec.lock`. I undid all of that, so the only changes are the two screen files and the new `ANSWER.md`. Nothing is committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":193,"cache_read_input_tokens":32411,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":193},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d5a305eb-d1f0-489f-a819-97e1c7c58467","uuid":"04e30a60-62bc-45dd-8583-6feb68afcea9","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:09:17.326Z","request_id":"req_011CgS1Lb93nkYL2h2mobDDs"}
